# Event Publisher — agent gates

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before editing production code.

## Codebase

- Production code lives under `src/` and is loaded from `event-publisher-on-aws.php`. Do not add new root-level PHP files.
- Put AWS HTTP/signing in `EventBridgePutEvents`. Put WordPress hooks and admin UI in `EventBridgePostEvents`.

## Static checks (run before claiming done)

- `npm run agent:check` must pass.
- After PHP changes, run `npm run test:unit` and `npm run test:integration` when wp-env is available.

## Forbidden slop

- Do not add packages to `composer.json` `require` (only `php` is allowed).
- Do not commit `vendor/` or add production Composer dependencies.
- Do not add unsolicited markdown in the repo root (except when the user asks for docs).
- Do not add long justification comments for shortcuts; fix the root cause or add a test/lint.
- Do not copy timer/workaround patterns from other projects; this plugin has no renderer/main split.

## Tests

- Prefer `tests/integration/` for behavior that touches WordPress options, cron, or post transitions.
- Mock HTTP with patterns from `tests/fixtures/aws-responses.php` and `pre_http_request` filters.